2 8. Section 127 Cr.P.C., provides for alteration of maintenance allowance in the following circumstances:-
(i) The Magistrate finds that competent civil court has passed any order due to which maintenance allowance granted has to be cancelled or modified;
(ii) The woman in whose favour maintenance allowance has been provided, has remarried after obtaining divorce such order of maintenance can be cancelled from the date of her remarriage;
(iii) Such woman has received whole of the sum which, under any customary or personal law applicable to the parties, was payable on such divorce;
(iv) The woman has obtained divorce from her husband and she had voluntarily surrendered her rights to maintenance or interim maintenance, as the case may be,
after her divorce, cancel the order from the date thereof.
9. The alteration of maintenance allowance under Section 127 Cr.P.C. can be done by the trial Court on the ground of change of circumstances as mentioned in that section.
